DESCRIPTION:International Stout Day is kept in early November — November 
 5 in 2026 — and it has something most observances of its kind do not: a 
 founder who says so in print. The beer writer Erin Peters\, who publishes 
 as The Beer Goddess\, created it\, and wrote in 2017 that the year's editi
 on was the seventh annual. The beer is much older\, and its name is older 
 still: "stout" began as a word for strong beer\, attached itself to porter
 \, and ended up meaning something porter is not.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrate
 s.com/holiday/international-stout-day/
